warning[NK1233]: `id[…]` names a type the arguments of the call already say.
  --> tests/type_arguments_warned.nika:9:5
   |
 9 |     println(id[i64](3))
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = note: Brackets after a function's name are allowed while their uses are collected; here the arguments already say the type.
   = help: Leave the brackets out, `id(…)`, or add your use case to https://github.com/Nikaia-Language/Nikaia/issues/514.
